{"study_accession":"PRJNA892941","secondary_study_accession":"SRP403909","title":"HDAC1 regulates the chromatin landscape to control transcriptional dependencies in chronic lymphocytic leukemia [RNA-seq]","description":"Chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL) is a quiescent B-cell malignancy that depends on transcriptional dysregulation for survival. The histone deacetylases are transcriptional regulators whose role within the regulatory chromatin and consequence on the CLL transcriptome is poorly characterized. Here, we profiled and integrated the genome wide occupancy of HDAC1, BRD4, H3K27Ac and H3K9Ac signals with chromatin accessibility, Pol2 occupancy and target expression signatures in CLL cells. We identified that when HDAC1 was recruited within super-enhancers (SEs) marked by acetylated H3K27 and BRD4, it functioned as a transcriptional activator that drove the de novo expression of select genes to facilitate survival and progression in CLL. Targeting HDACs reduced BRD4 and Pol2 engagement to downregulate the transcript and proteins levels of specific oncogenic driver genes in CLL such as BLK, a key mediator of the B-cell receptor pathway, core transcription factors such as PAX5 and IKZF3 and the anti-apoptotic gene, BCL2. Concurrently, HDAC1, when recruited in the absence of super-enhancers repressed target gene expression. HDAC inhibition reversed silencing of a defined set of protein coding and noncoding RNA genes. We focused on a specific set of microRNA genes and show that their upregulation was inversely correlated with the expression of CLL specific survival, transcription factor and signaling genes. Our findings identify that the transcriptional activator and repressor functions of HDACs cooperate within the same tumor to establish the transcriptional dependencies essential for survival in CLL. Overall design: CLL samples (untreated or exposed to 400mM abexinostat) were harvested after 24h of drug exposure, extracted for total RNA and libraries prepared and seqeuenced by total RNA Seq","pubmed":"36287107","geo_series":"","n_samples":20,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN31401925","study_accession":"PRJNA892941","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"RNA-seq_s1124C","description":"RNA-seq_s1124C","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM6666042","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2022-10-26","attributes":[["source_name","CLL,1124, Control"],["tissue","Blood, PBMC"],["cell_type","Human peripheral blood mononuclear cells"],["genotype","del 13 q"],["disease","CLL"],["treatment","control"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR22002020","experiment_accession":"SRX17984427","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 4000","read_count":53384926,"base_count":5288686395,"first_public":"2022-10-26","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 4000 sequencing: GSM6666042: RNA-seq_s1124C Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN31401926","study_accession":"PRJNA892941","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"RNA-seq_s1124A","description":"RNA-seq_s1124A","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM6666041","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2022-10-26","attributes":[["source_name","CLL,1124, Abexinostat 400mM 24h"],["tissue","Blood, PBMC"],["cell_type","Human peripheral blood mononuclear cells"],["genotype","del 13 q"],["disease","CLL"],["treatment","HDAC inhibitor, Abexinostat 400mM, 24h"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR22002021","experiment_accession":"SRX17984426","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 4000","read_count":59346366,"base_count":5878277612,"first_public":"2022-10-26","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 4000 sequencing: GSM6666041: RNA-seq_s1124A Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN31401927","study_accession":"PRJNA892941","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"RNA-seq_s1119C","description":"R